<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Tactical Advantage</title><link>http://localhost:1313/</link><description>Recent content on Tactical Advantage</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><atom:link href="http://localhost:1313/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Claim eCash</title><link>http://localhost:1313/claim-ecash/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>http://localhost:1313/claim-ecash/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;On October 31, 2026, Bitcoin is scheduled to undergo a hard fork called &lt;a href="https://ecash.com/"&gt;eCash&lt;/a&gt;. At the fork block, BTC holders will be credited ECX at 1:1 ratio. To claim it, you must control the keys for the wallet that held the BTC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As of &lt;strong&gt;v4&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;a href="http://localhost:1313/ewallet/"&gt;eWallet&lt;/a&gt; provides a simple way to claim ECX for Bitcoin holders, and this guide walks you through the process.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>eWallet</title><link>http://localhost:1313/ewallet/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>http://localhost:1313/ewallet/</guid><description/></item></channel></rss>